        "description": "Presence of nystagmus, reduced visual acuity, and photophobia",
        "category": "minor",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      },
      {
        "id": "family-history",
        "description": "Consanguinity or family history consistent with autosomal recessive inheritance",
        "category": "supportive",
        "requiredForDiagnosis": false
      }
    ],
    "minimumForDiagnosis": "Presence of characteristic hypopigmentation of skin, hair, and eyes plus identification of pathogenic TYRP1 mutation",
    "notes": "Genetic testing is essential for definitive diagnosis due to phenotypic overlap with other OCA types."
